TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC: make the CSIPHY talk

WHY
---
The front sensor is transmitting -confirmed by reading it over I2C while it is
running: mode 0x0103, 4 D-PHY lanes, 2592 wide- and not a single frame comes
out of CAMSS. And there is not one error message, because mainline MASKS every
CSIPHY interrupt in csiphy_lanes_enable(). So a link that does not lock fails
in absolute silence and leaves no trace.

Everything from the CSID downwards is already ruled out, with proof: the CSID's
internal pattern generator captures 5 frames at 2592x1940 through csid0 ->
vfe0_rdi0 -> /dev/video0. The fault is in the stretch
sensor -> CSIPHY1 -> CSID.

Trying to read the CSIPHY registers from user space is NO GOOD: with
CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM the reads through /dev/mem silently return zeros. It was
checked by reading the VFE0 version, which the driver reports as 1.3.0 and
which comes out as 0x00000000 through /dev/mem. An instrument that lies.

WHAT IT DOES
------------
1. It unmasks the CSIPHY interrupts, so that the ISR that already exists can
   tell what it sees on the lanes.
2. It logs which parameters the PHY is programmed with: link frequency, timer
   clock, settle count, lane mask.
3. The ISR prints the eleven status registers, capped at 20 times in case the
   link is noisy and fires without stopping.

This does NOT fix anything: it is for looking. It comes out when the cause is
known.
